      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The case is reported of a patient with a rectus abdominis syndrome. Attention is drawn to the possibility that patients with abdominal pain, in whom no intra-abdominal cause is found, may suffer from this presumed nerve entrapment syndrome. No surgery is required and therapy can be simple."},
